note for test at the latch on a ulong counter (type 5, the largest unsigned type) above 2^63 (B.LO, not
note B.LT): the first pass sets i to 2^64 - 2, the latch adds 1 and 2^64 - 1 is not below 3, so 1 pass
note (exit 1); a signed latch test reads -1 and runs -1, 0, 1, 2 too (exit 5).
om2
fn main to int
n = long 0
for i ulong 3
if eq n 0
i = ulong 18446744073709551614
end
n = add n 1
end
ret int n
end
